findings.body:
`SettingsTextFormatter.formatStudiesText` passes `strings.detailTextStudies`, which is the v136 key `Settings.detailTextStudies` ("may install and run studies from time to time"). The PR adds `detailTextStudiesV2` for the v148 copy, but the formatter never uses it. Once someone wires the formatter into the "Allow Feature Studies" toggle, the label and the subtitle will disagree.

::diff{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="418-431"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The Rollouts method correctly uses `detailTextRollouts`. Only the Studies method has the stale key.

::suggestion{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="423-425"}
        func formatStudiesText(appName: String) -> String {
            return String(format: strings.detailTextStudiesV2, appName)
        }

The PR adds five Focus keys: `Settings.toggleStudies.v2`, `Settings.detailTextStudies.v2`, `Settings.toggleRollouts`, `Settings.detailTextRollouts`, and `Settings.detailTextSendUsageData.v2`. None of them appear in `focus-ios/Blockzilla/en-US.lproj/Localizable.strings`, and none appear in any other locale. The v1 equivalents are in the en-US file (lines 329, 332, and 449).

`NSLocalizedString` falls back to the inline `value`, so nothing crashes. But once these constants are wired up, every locale will show the English copy until the keys are added to the source file and translated. The `detailTextSendUsageDataV2` value is also identical to the v1 copy, so it adds a key with no change in text.

::code{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="203-209"}

A repo-wide search finds no references to `labelStudiesV2`, `detailTextStudiesV2`, `labelRollouts`, `detailTextRollouts`, `detailTextSendUsageDataV2`, or `SettingsTextFormatter`. `SettingsViewController` still uses `labelStudies` and `detailTextStudies`. The new class also uses a singleton pattern (`static let shared` plus `private init`) that the rest of this namespace does not need, and it adds behavior to `UIConstants`, which is otherwise a set of constants.

The PR checklist asks for tests on new code, and this formatter has none. Its Studies method is also wrong (see the finding on the v1 key).

::code{file="focus-ios/Blockzilla/UIComponents/UIConstants.swift" lines="418-431"}

The PR adds `firefox-ios.xliff:Settings.Studies.Message.v148` to the quotes exclusions. The value is `%@ randomly selects users to test features, which improves quality for everyone.`, which contains no quote characters. An exclusion on a string the check would not flag either does nothing or hides a flag the author did not intend to hide. No comment explains it.

I could not confirm the linter's exact rule from the repo, so the author should confirm whether the exclusion is needed. If it is not, removing it keeps the suppressions list honest.

::diff{file=".github/l10n/linter_config_ios.json" lines="5-12"}
